{"thought":"I need to find Alex Yoong's races with round < 20. Let me write a Python script to process both CSV files and join them.","action":"execute_python","action_input":{"code":"import csv\n\n# Read driverStandings for Alex Yoong (driverId=62)\nyoong_races = []\nwith open('csv/driverStandings.csv', 'r') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        if row['driverId'] == '62':\n            yoong_races.append(row['raceId'])\n\nprint(f\"Alex Yoong raceIds: {yoong_races}\")\n\n# Read races.csv and filter by round < 20\nraces_data = {}\nwith open('csv/races.csv', 'r') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        races_data[row['raceId']] = row\n\n# Find races where Alex Yoong participated and round < 20\nresult = []\nfor raceId in yoong_races:\n    if raceId in races_data:\n        race = races_data[raceId]\n        round_num = int(race['round'])\n        if round_num < 20:\n            result.append({'raceId': raceId, 'name': race['name'], 'round': round_num})\n\nprint(f\"Races with round < 20: {result}\")"}}
